WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:13.855
Sign in as the business owner.

2
00:00:13.955 --> 00:00:20.199
A stock take is a guided count of what is really on your shelves. Open Inventory, then Stock Takes.

3
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:22.600
Click New stock take.

4
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.855
Choose the branch you are counting. Camp is already selected.

5
00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:32.761
Count the whole branch, or just one category. Choose One category to keep this count short.

6
00:00:32.861 --> 00:00:35.176
Pick the category to count.

7
00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:37.659
Click Start counting.

8
00:00:37.759 --> 00:00:44.281
The sheet lists every product to count. The system quantity is hidden, so you count what you really see.

9
00:00:44.381 --> 00:00:47.766
Type the quantity you counted for each product.

10
00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:52.846
Click Save counts. You can leave and come back later, saved counts are kept.

11
00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:58.163
When everything is counted, click Review differences.

12
00:00:58.263 --> 00:01:03.134
Here you see the shortage and the surplus, and each difference by product.

13
00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:12.167
If the numbers look right, click Approve and update stock. Your stock now matches the shelf.

14
00:01:14.768 --> 00:01:20.079
The stock take is now finished. Open Stock levels to see the corrected quantities.

15
00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.281
Search for the pens.

16
00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:29.617
Run a stock take regularly to catch loss, damage and counting mistakes early.
